WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:02.360
Hardening depends on maintained software.

00:00:02.580 --> 00:00:06.900
Operating systems, firmware, third-party applications, packages, drivers,

00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:09.200
and endpoint agents all age.

00:00:09.420 --> 00:00:14.620
Vendors release updates to correct defects, improve reliability, and reduce known risk.

00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:19.080
A system with missing patches, unsupported software, unmanaged packages,

00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:23.460
or outdated firmware can become difficult to defend and difficult to recover.

00:00:23.680 --> 00:00:26.560
Software inventory supports patching decisions.

00:00:26.780 --> 00:00:31.100
Teams need to know what is installed, where it came from, whether it is still supported,

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:32.760
and who owns it.

00:00:32.980 --> 00:00:37.460
Package sources and software deployment methods should be controlled so systems do not

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:39.680
accumulate unmanaged tools.

00:00:39.900 --> 00:00:43.900
Unsupported software should be replaced, upgraded, isolated,

00:00:44.120 --> 00:00:47.800
or formally tracked as an exception with compensating controls.

00:00:48.020 --> 00:00:51.860
Endpoint protection is part of the hardening baseline, not a checkbox.

00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:56.800
Antivirus, EDR, application control, host firewall policy,

00:00:57.020 --> 00:01:01.740
and related controls should be enabled, monitored, and configured according to policy.

00:01:01.960 --> 00:01:04.840
A deployed agent that is disabled, unhealthy,

00:01:05.060 --> 00:01:07.940
or not sending alerts may give a false sense of protection.

00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:12.240
SOC and endpoint teams should know how health and alerting are reviewed.

00:01:12.460 --> 00:01:15.340
Patch rollout must be balanced with availability.

00:01:15.560 --> 00:01:20.600
Test updates, stage deployment, schedule maintenance windows when needed, monitor results,

00:01:20.820 --> 00:01:22.900
and retain rollback options.

00:01:23.120 --> 00:01:27.440
Some systems cannot patch immediately, but every delay should be visible and owned.

00:01:27.660 --> 00:01:32.060
Patching is strongest when it is connected to inventory, classification,

00:01:32.280 --> 00:01:35.400
endpoint protection, backups, and change control.
